This project is for a mount that can track orbiting satellites across the sky along a full 180 degree arc, which can
accompany a broad range of objects mounted (ideally a camera).
Specifications are below:


R_ID 1: Speed. Must be fast enough to track LEO objects (ISS will be used as a benchmark). The exact angular speed of
this will be later derived.

R_ID 2: Accuracy. A reasonable accuracy for tracking will be later derived during a trade study

R_ID 3: Functionality. Must be able to sweep 180 degrees of skyline without impediment or any manual manipulation, and
support a camera

R_ID 4: Must be able to support a few flame stickers on it (sick as hell)


Success criteria will be determined based on the ability of the mount to track the ISS primarily, but due to
circumstantiality of ISS flyovers the moon will serve as a secondary benchmark.


